 @Rocket-yc8pj  Some local markets give you better opportunities. I have a Microcenter near me and I had been looking for an XTX for a few months. I usually log in a couple of times a week to look for open box specials along with their store credit card deals. They had a Sapphire Pulse 7900 XTX for $713 as an open box, bare card, no accessories or pretty OEM box included. The sealed box was on sale for $950. They do have another open box in stock with the box and accessories for $854 at the Fairfax, VA store. For $140 less though, I went with the plain card and no box or accessories. 

This week Microcenter had a special where if you bought any monitor you got 10% off the total purchase in the same order, or 24 months no interest. I take the 10%. Also they offer 5% off on everyday purchases as a perk for having their credit card, which covers most of the sales tax for normal purchases. I found an open box portable monitor for $59 which I planned to buy anyway to use for work. So $6 off the monitor and $71 off the XTX after the 10% credit card discount took it down to $642, or $17 off the $702 for the card and a free portable monitor depending on how you look at it.   

Best Buy open boxes are many times great deals as well. I built a new Plex server and put an open box RTX 4060 in it for the AV1+Nvenc capabilities. I found it after a couple of months of looking for an open box deal and scored a plain-Jane, no RGB, dual fan Gigabyte Windforce card for $240.

