if I must give some constructive feedback:
1) it is to include 1080Ti in the flagship comparisons.
2) 16:30 regarding the remark on 1% and 0.1% lows. If there is an inherent error on these calculations, why still show them? ... or visualize the error on the measurement together with the actual measurement. The 3 numbers at the end of the bars also distract from the main message when max fps and 1% and 0.1% lows are close together, as they overlap. I think for shooters specifically frame time consistency does matter as they do affect your aim, even at higher fps. .. well at least in CSGO it does. Perhaps other simulation/racing or fighting games which require a fast input could also benefit. I would rethink how these numbers are represented. Perhaps log these numbers per title somewhere that in case someone wants to have a look at a specific title they can still can... but for the video and main message bundle them in a consolidated metric or metrics.

