 @Wobbothe3rd  2080 ti user here who games a whole lot, I'm tired of people claiming DLSS "Looks better than native" - I'm also sick of DLSS artifacts.

Sure if a game runs so poorly that Native means 40 FPS or less I'll use DLSS but ONLY because I have to. What we want is native quality and everyone knows it. DLSS is cool for rendering the game at 4k/5k and then setting it to quality/balanced mode (Still rendering equal to or above native res) and then you can actually surpass Native quality but again that still introduces artifacts that are foreign to a native image....

DLSS is a crutch we need only because Ray Tracing hardware just isn't there yet.

